WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.770
Some people wait for the perfect setup.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.190
Arjun doesn't.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.790
Introducing Arjun Mishra.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.950
He wanted to build for iPhone.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.470
He didn't own a Mac.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.870
So the cloud became his Mac.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.070
On GitHub's macOS runners, his app is built, tested, signed,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.150
and shipped to the App Store, all from a Windows PC.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.790
That app is Roadpack: one live trip for every car in the group,

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.710
kept in sync in real time, even when the signal drops.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.990
And it lives where you look: in Live Activities,

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.430
the Dynamic Island, widgets, and Siri.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.870
Three releases in,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.830
a paying subscriber within the first six downloads, before any marketing.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.150
Then he co-founded Mune,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:53.470
a finance app where every AI answer happens on your iPhone.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.830
With Apple's MLX, a 4-billion-parameter model runs right on the device.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.710
And it doesn't just answer. It acts.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.950
Checking what you can afford, building budgets, setting goals,

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.940
all from one conversation.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.780
At UBC, his research asks a bigger question.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.980
Can AI agents check the web for accessibility?

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:19.300
His forty agents found 86% of real issues.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.100
A standard checker? 36%.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:26.420
First author. Submitted to CHI 2027.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.020
At IFS Copperleaf, his co-op became a part-time role,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.660
building data pipelines and a return-on-investment portal for senior leadership.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.860
And away from the keyboard?

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.620
He flies drones over Fuji and Vancouver's fireworks.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.820
He hikes. Builds LEGO Technic.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.160
And has two hackathon prizes.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.520
Oh. One more thing.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.890
Arjun Mishra.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.050
Available May 2027.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.810
For software, forward-deployed, and AI engineering roles.
